    "id": "b28d63549f04a619d24f155c",
    "path": "datafusion_common::utils::memory::RecordBatchMemoryCounter",
    "name": "RecordBatchMemoryCounter",
    "owner": null,
    "crate": "datafusion-common",
    "version": "55.1.0",
    "kind": "struct",
    "signature": "struct RecordBatchMemoryCounter",
    "docs": "Tracks the memory used by a sequence of [`RecordBatch`]es that may share\nunderlying buffers, counting each buffer exactly once.\n\nUse this instead of [`get_record_batch_memory_size`] to account for the\ntotal memory of a sequence of batches, e.g. when buffering the batches of\nan input stream. Such batches can share buffers (for example, operators\nlike aggregates emit one large batch as multiple zero-copy slices), and\ncalling [`get_record_batch_memory_size`] per batch counts the shared\nbuffers once per batch, while this counter counts them exactly once. A\nbatch's buffers are kept alive by the batch even when only a sub-range is\nreferenced, so counting unique buffers in full reflects the memory the\nbatches actually retain.",
    "span": {
      "filename": "src/utils/memory.rs",
